  "details": "When getting an invite and you select reply and add a picture, and reverse the camera to look at yourself, after the picture is taken the image isn't flipped horizontally, but should be\n\nA very minor thing, but common convention would be to flip the image horizontally _after_ its taken so it looks \"right\" and text is readable when looking at it\n\nFor example, on any modern smart phone when you're taking a selfie picture it shows a mirror of yourself, but once the picture is taken the image is flipped horizontally afterwards so it looks \"right\"\n\nI selected all platforms, albeit only testing on PC. Just an assumption",
